# `hound.use()` — global middleware

Register middleware that wraps every job handler execution. Runs in
registration order; `next()` continues the chain. Throwing or skipping
`next()` short-circuits the handler and fails the job.

```ts
hound.use(async (ctx, next) => {
  const span = tracer.startSpan(ctx.name);
  try {
    await next();
    span.setStatus({ code: SpanStatusCode.OK });
  } catch (err) {
    span.recordException(err);
    throw err;
  } finally {
    span.end();
  }
});

`Parcel.readSerializable()` was deprecated in Android API 33 (TIRAMISU) in favor of the type-safe `readSerializable(ClassLoader, Class)` overload. The KSP code generator was unconditionally emitting the deprecated call for all `Serializable` types.

## Changes

- **`builder/Parcel.kt`**: For `ParcelableType.Serializable`, emit an API-level branch instead of a bare `readSerializable()` cast. Uses `checkNotNull` on both paths for consistent null-handling (matching the existing `Parcelable` case).
- **`KaidlProcessorTest.kt`**: Extend `androidStubsSource` with `android.os.Build` stub and the new `readSerializable(ClassLoader?, Class<T>)` / `writeSerializable` signatures on `Parcel`; add a dedicated test for the Serializable codegen path.

**Generated code (before → after):**

```kotlin
// Before
val uuid: UUID = `data`.readSerializable() as UUID

// After
val uuid: UUID = if (android.os.Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= android.os.Build.VERSION_CODES.TIRAMISU) {
    checkNotNull(`data`.readSerializable(null, UUID::class.java))
} else {
    @Suppress("DEPRECATION") checkNotNull(`data`.readSerializable()) as UUID
}
```

The `null` ClassLoader matches the internal behavior of the deprecated `readSerializable()`, which also passes `null` as the loader.

